1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,320
Rathal saw at once that the Unsullied Flame was a gift from the Great Soul.

2
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:19,780
He resolved to harness its power with technology and created Amaterasu.

3
00:00:21,260 --> 00:00:26,040
By the light of Amaterasu's sacred flame, the people began to rebuild.

4
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:30,280
With its power, they established a new state in the Far East.

5
00:00:50,760 --> 00:00:52,860
Looks like an old subway station.

6
00:00:56,040 --> 00:01:07,100
That was powerful.

7
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:09,440
It burned through my coat instantly.

8
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:12,820
Where's the shooter?

9
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:14,920
I haven't heard a sound.

10
00:01:16,060 --> 00:01:17,800
But somewhere in the dark.

11
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:25,940
The young man with the Adola burst, the flame meant to exterminate mankind.

12
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:28,220
He doesn't belong with you.

13
00:01:28,940 --> 00:01:31,340
I'd like to thank you for bringing him to us.

14
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:33,000
You've saved us some trouble.

15
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:36,580
What do you intend to do with Shinra?

16
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:38,360
Tell me your objective.

17
00:01:38,360 --> 00:01:44,240
Die.

18
00:01:48,240 --> 00:01:48,640
Die.

19
00:01:50,180 --> 00:01:50,380
Die.

20
00:01:50,380 --> 00:02:18,860
Take what you got and leave now

21
00:02:18,860 --> 00:02:20,820
You're wearing out your welcome

22
00:02:20,820 --> 00:02:23,300
No one here wants to see you

23
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:24,440
Here, yeah

24
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:26,860
Think that you won from day one

25
00:02:26,860 --> 00:02:28,900
But the devil will come

26
00:02:28,900 --> 00:02:31,160
You know just why he wants you

27
00:02:31,160 --> 00:02:32,520
Don't you?

28
00:02:32,740 --> 00:02:34,500
Your crooked desire

29
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:36,300
Left us in history

30
00:02:36,300 --> 00:02:38,560
Miscuited, defighted

31
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:40,280
In the part of the razor

32
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:42,380
You started a fighter

33
00:02:42,380 --> 00:02:44,740
You gotta watch it burn

34
00:02:44,740 --> 00:02:47,660
Try to save yourself like you always do

35
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:51,080
Every bridge we build

36
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:53,540
You think it's just a burn it down

37
00:02:53,540 --> 00:02:55,900
Just burn it down

38
00:02:55,900 --> 00:02:58,800
When everything is gone

39
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:01,580
You wish you only heard us out

40
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:03,240
Heard us out

41
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:04,080
Screaming

42
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:07,000
Mkay Shiestion

43
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:09,500
Mkay!

44
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:09,800
Mkay!

45
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:09,920
Mkay!

46
00:03:12,220 --> 00:03:12,720
Mkay!

47
00:03:16,460 --> 00:03:16,840
Mkay!

48
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:17,500
Mkay!

49
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:17,860
Mkay!

50
00:03:18,020 --> 00:03:18,260
Mkay!

51
00:03:18,260 --> 00:03:18,320
Mkay!

52
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:18,760
Mkay!

53
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:18,820
Mkay!

54
00:03:19,820 --> 00:03:20,440
Mkay!

55
00:03:20,440 --> 00:03:21,000
Mkay!

56
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:21,480
Mkay!

57
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:21,820
Mkay!

58
00:03:21,820 --> 00:03:22,380
Mkay!

59
00:03:22,380 --> 00:03:22,560
Mkay!

60
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:22,680
Went!

61
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:23,720
Where are you?

62
00:03:24,460 --> 00:03:26,400
I'm completely cut off from the others

63
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:28,420
And the enemy could appear at any second

64
00:03:28,420 --> 00:03:31,780
I'm stays on his toes man

65
00:03:31,780 --> 00:03:34,280
Hold it.

66
00:03:35,900 --> 00:03:37,080
You okay, Leaked?

67
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:38,740
Don't move a muscle.

68
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:40,780
To be honest, Shinra, I...

69
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:42,020
I've been better.

70
00:03:42,580 --> 00:03:44,760
You're the one with the Adola Burst, right?

71
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:48,520
If you value this man's life, you'll do as I tell you.

72
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:50,760
Hurry, Shinra! Use the rabbit!

73
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:52,780
You know...

74
00:03:52,780 --> 00:03:53,820
The tiger hand sign?

75
00:03:53,820 --> 00:03:54,360
Be quiet!

76
00:04:02,660 --> 00:04:04,760
That's some pretty impressive speed.

77
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:06,260
The rapid, you said?

78
00:04:06,820 --> 00:04:09,060
That's even cooler than kicker man kick.

79
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:13,500
With my rapid man kick, I can't be beat!

80
00:04:14,260 --> 00:04:16,900
I think Captain Shinmon's gonna shoot that down, too.

81
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:18,880
Why do you keep throwing man into everything?

82
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:21,700
One word. Shinra bansho.

83
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:23,640
It means all of nature.

84
00:04:24,760 --> 00:04:27,700
And well, since the bond can also be pronounced as man...

85
00:04:28,300 --> 00:04:29,120
There's me!

86
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:30,740
My little brother!

87
00:04:31,780 --> 00:04:33,280
And then, man!

88
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:34,780
Right smack between us!

89
00:04:35,080 --> 00:04:37,480
When we bond together, we're Shinra bansho!

90
00:04:38,660 --> 00:04:40,580
That's why I'm says man a lot, man.

91
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:42,000
Makes perfect sense.

92
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:44,240
You should explain it to Shinmon like that.

93
00:04:44,280 --> 00:04:45,340
I'm sure it'll go great.

94
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:51,200
Sounds like Lieutenant Hinoa.

95
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:52,300
We should go.

96
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:54,580
The others are fighting the white-clad, too.

97
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:57,880
The more goons we beat, the less they'll have to.

98
00:05:01,780 --> 00:05:12,460
It seems my position has been compromised.

99
00:05:12,460 --> 00:05:20,960
Snipers using the darkness as cover between attacks, and their fire's too bright to trace back to them.

100
00:05:20,960 --> 00:05:27,300
I used ricochet control to pepper a wide area, but there's no sign I made contact.

101
00:05:28,300 --> 00:05:30,540
Can't get a clean shot with all these obstructions.

102
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:31,980
I should close in.

103
00:05:31,980 --> 00:05:39,220
At any rate, the enemy knows where I am.

104
00:05:39,860 --> 00:05:40,680
I need to move.

105
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:43,860
No cover in here.

106
00:05:44,280 --> 00:05:46,180
I need to get through as fast as I can.

107
00:05:46,180 --> 00:05:50,920
The moment he gives us an opening, we'll attack.

108
00:05:51,180 --> 00:05:52,660
He's fighting arrow, remember?

109
00:05:53,140 --> 00:05:55,260
I doubt that we'll get the chance to do anything.

110
00:05:56,040 --> 00:05:57,640
We're both using ranged weapons.

111
00:05:58,400 --> 00:06:02,160
But since I have my ricochet control, I should have the advantage up close.

112
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:06,440
Did you come in here to try and escape from my arrows?

113
00:06:06,440 --> 00:06:09,600
How ironic.

114
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:11,880
All you did was trap yourself.

115
00:06:12,660 --> 00:06:13,060
Break.

116
00:06:15,440 --> 00:06:15,940
Damn!

117
00:06:15,940 --> 00:06:32,720
I've stumbled into your hunting ground.

118
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:35,620
That's right, and I never let my prey escape.

119
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:38,360
I will be taking the Adola Burst as well.

120
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:46,320
Your brainwashed zealots, who can't see the value of a human life.

121
00:06:46,780 --> 00:06:48,160
Shinra would never help you.

122
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:51,680
This scorched world is in a constant state of flux.

123
00:06:52,020 --> 00:06:54,640
It's on the cusp of a great upheaval as we speak.

124
00:06:55,320 --> 00:06:58,300
And in the wake of it, all our feelings will amount to nothing.

125
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:05,680
Those who insist that their existence has meaning are fools who can't conform themselves to this world.

126
00:07:05,680 --> 00:07:09,840
You say Shinra would never help us, as if he has a choice.

127
00:07:10,340 --> 00:07:11,680
But his feelings don't matter.

128
00:07:12,880 --> 00:07:16,220
The evangelist requires that young man's Adola Burst.

129
00:07:16,740 --> 00:07:18,180
So we will take it.

130
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:21,440
When you look at yourself as a member of a group,

131
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:24,540
your feelings as an individual lose importance.

132
00:07:25,340 --> 00:07:29,100
When that group's the size of a country or the world, that gets truer.

133
00:07:30,180 --> 00:07:34,400
At any second, those you care for could burst into flames right in front of you.

134
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:38,880
So it's probably for the best, if you forego all attachments.

135
00:07:39,620 --> 00:07:45,040
And fulfill your dispassionate role as an insignificant cog in the machine of our society.

136
00:07:45,440 --> 00:07:46,780
One that feels nothing.

137
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:50,960
There are many people, including me, who think that way.

138
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:53,520
It's certainly an easier way to live.

139
00:07:54,160 --> 00:07:56,120
Emotions can be downright exhausting.

140
00:07:56,120 --> 00:07:59,980
If that's how you see things, why fight?

141
00:08:03,080 --> 00:08:05,860
First you tell me my soldier's feelings don't matter.

142
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:08,620
Then you expect me to hand him over?

143
00:08:08,860 --> 00:08:10,020
What do you take me for?

144
00:08:11,500 --> 00:08:14,080
Philosophy aside, you spit fuel in my face?

145
00:08:16,380 --> 00:08:18,900
You'd better expect me to get fired up.

146
00:08:18,900 --> 00:08:29,320
Now that's a spectacle.

147
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:33,840
It makes a devastating roar.

148
00:08:34,520 --> 00:08:36,620
And a devastating shockwave, too.

149
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:38,260
I don't get it.

150
00:08:38,380 --> 00:08:39,740
What the hell is he firing?

151
00:08:39,740 --> 00:08:50,500
These are just standard 7.62x51mm bullets.

152
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:52,600
But with all my power behind them.

153
00:08:53,480 --> 00:08:56,180
They move so fast that I don't need to score a hit.

154
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:58,800
This sonic boom will do plenty of damage.

155
00:09:00,560 --> 00:09:03,920
He destroys another gun barrel every time he pulls that trigger.

156
00:09:04,720 --> 00:09:06,580
He makes that gun shoot like a cannon.

157
00:09:06,580 --> 00:09:08,420
I wonder if Arrow's all right.

158
00:09:18,300 --> 00:09:21,260
I was looking for an opportunity to finish him.

159
00:09:21,700 --> 00:09:25,120
But that would be like stepping into a shootout between a pair of tanks!

160
00:09:32,120 --> 00:09:33,720
My strength is spent.

161
00:09:34,860 --> 00:09:36,300
Vision's fading fast.

162
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:39,460
It feels like my eyelids are melting.

163
00:09:40,940 --> 00:09:43,480
I can feel my consciousness drifting away.

164
00:09:45,280 --> 00:09:47,940
Through the dust and darkness of this underground hell,

165
00:09:48,680 --> 00:09:51,060
all that I can make out is the smell of gunpowder.

166
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:55,580
What's become of...

167
00:09:56,880 --> 00:09:58,380
the other shooter?

168
00:09:58,380 --> 00:10:07,500
When people can burst into flames at random and lose their lives in an instant.

169
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:11,660
Becoming indifferent about your own life

170
00:10:11,660 --> 00:10:14,860
is a way of devoting yourself to the world.

171
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:19,080
My death won't change a thing.

172
00:10:19,080 --> 00:10:33,020
Damn you, Obi.

173
00:10:34,360 --> 00:10:38,720
Making me a lieutenant when the 8th is barely even big enough to call a company.

174
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:42,080
I'd feel guilty leaving you to run things on your own.

175
00:10:42,080 --> 00:10:47,480
If I die down here, then who's gonna teach our rookies discipline?

176
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:53,840
Know why you couldn't finish me off?

177
00:10:53,840 --> 00:10:56,720
It's because your first shot hit the wrong shoulder.

178
00:10:57,280 --> 00:11:00,400
I won't go down while I wear the emblem of Company 8!

179
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:04,560
I'll use her flames...

180
00:11:04,560 --> 00:11:07,920
to make it go even faster!

181
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:30,180
That took a lot out of me.

182
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:33,040
Doubt I'll be able to move for a while.

183
00:11:34,560 --> 00:11:35,340
It's funny.

184
00:11:35,340 --> 00:11:39,080
I thought that push-past-your-limits stuff

185
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:41,380
was just a fantasy for gullible kids.

186
00:11:48,060 --> 00:11:50,640
You're the ones behind the fog and the shimmers.

187
00:11:51,520 --> 00:11:54,700
Guess you finally think you can take me, you cowards.

188
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:58,840
Striking the enemy when they're at their weakest is Tactics 101.

189
00:11:59,580 --> 00:12:01,860
Arrow was best suited to wear you down.

190
00:12:05,340 --> 00:12:09,080
So how does it feel to know that you'll soon die at this coward's hand?

191
00:12:09,080 --> 00:12:12,180
I doubt you have the strength to offer any resistance.

192
00:12:12,760 --> 00:12:14,360
Let me put you to rest.

193
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:25,200
You would have done me in with that.

194
00:12:25,540 --> 00:12:26,960
A shame it was only a shimmer.

195
00:12:27,500 --> 00:12:28,240
Now die.

196
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:31,380
That was surprisingly powerful for a last-ditch effort.

197
00:12:31,820 --> 00:12:33,540
Not that it matters when you miss.

198
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:38,280
No.

199
00:12:38,980 --> 00:12:40,420
I hit my mark.

200
00:12:40,420 --> 00:12:59,460
Though I am descended from the heavens,

201
00:12:59,860 --> 00:13:01,700
I was born from the earth below.

202
00:13:02,160 --> 00:13:04,160
I transverse the land and sky.

203
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:08,220
I'm a knight.

204
00:13:12,060 --> 00:13:15,460
I saw Arthur watching us through a tiny crack in the ceiling.

205
00:13:16,220 --> 00:13:17,700
Signaled him to come on down.

206
00:13:17,700 --> 00:13:24,040
So you're the pure soul who summoned this heavenly champion down to earth.

207
00:13:24,340 --> 00:13:25,180
What do you need?

208
00:13:25,820 --> 00:13:27,180
Have a quest for me?

209
00:13:30,280 --> 00:13:32,820
Do I really have to explain the situation?

210
00:13:33,300 --> 00:13:33,920
You're good.

211
00:13:34,300 --> 00:13:35,640
His face was covered then.

212
00:13:35,900 --> 00:13:37,860
But I fought the shimmer guy at Vulcans.

213
00:13:38,760 --> 00:13:40,900
Why don't you handle this, Mirage?

214
00:13:41,580 --> 00:13:42,480
Not a problem.

215
00:13:43,100 --> 00:13:46,320
This one's more vulnerable to my shimmers than most.

216
00:13:50,460 --> 00:13:52,560
Kind of a one-trick pony, aren't you?

217
00:13:52,920 --> 00:13:56,380
This one trick has been the end of every foe I've met.

218
00:13:57,480 --> 00:13:57,960
Die!

219
00:13:57,960 --> 00:14:11,500
That attack was fake.

220
00:14:11,940 --> 00:14:13,700
It didn't have the breath of life in it.

221
00:14:14,480 --> 00:14:16,140
Let that stress heighten your awareness.

222
00:14:16,940 --> 00:14:18,060
Feel life around you.

223
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:20,840
Not just your allies, but your enemies, too.

224
00:14:21,560 --> 00:14:23,040
Focus on the lives at stake,

225
00:14:23,260 --> 00:14:25,520
and you can use the stress of the battle as a tool.

226
00:14:25,520 --> 00:14:28,740
Good. Don't let yourself fall prey to diversions for fate.

227
00:14:29,020 --> 00:14:31,680
You have to discern the attack that's coming to take your life.

228
00:14:33,340 --> 00:14:33,820
Focus.

229
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:36,040
Harness the tension you're feeling.

230
00:14:36,540 --> 00:14:37,880
Sense the life around you.

231
00:14:40,460 --> 00:14:42,720
Now that I've gained the wisdom of the samurai,

232
00:14:42,900 --> 00:14:44,520
I'm multi-classing as...

233
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:46,800
a knight samurai.

234
00:14:52,560 --> 00:14:53,240
Hold up.

235
00:14:54,040 --> 00:14:55,140
Let me think this through.

236
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:57,900
If I were a knight samurai,

237
00:14:58,220 --> 00:15:00,580
I'd be mostly a samurai, right?

238
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:02,220
That doesn't make sense.

239
00:15:05,220 --> 00:15:06,600
Oh, I had it backwards.

240
00:15:07,100 --> 00:15:07,740
I'm really...

241
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:09,820
a samurai knight.

242
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:16,980
Your eyes are great at tracking small movements.

243
00:15:17,300 --> 00:15:18,340
That can help you,

244
00:15:18,540 --> 00:15:19,760
or become a distraction.

245
00:15:19,760 --> 00:15:22,200
Be wary of deceptions and fates.

246
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:28,760
There's more out there than what the eye can see.

247
00:15:28,760 --> 00:15:32,320
Maybe he's just pretending he can see through my illusions,

248
00:15:32,780 --> 00:15:35,360
trusting I'd probe with my shimmers before attacking.

249
00:15:35,360 --> 00:15:36,740
In that case,

250
00:15:36,740 --> 00:15:39,740
with this large a number attacking en masse,

251
00:15:39,740 --> 00:15:42,480
he'll have to assume the real me is mixed in.

252
00:15:42,480 --> 00:15:44,860
But in truth,

253
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:46,480
all of them are fake.

254
00:15:46,480 --> 00:15:49,020
A real attack,

255
00:15:49,020 --> 00:15:50,980
the kind that's intended to take your life,

256
00:15:50,980 --> 00:15:52,780
always comes with a distinct breath.

257
00:15:53,440 --> 00:15:55,560
You need to listen for that breath of life.

258
00:15:57,360 --> 00:15:59,040
Like the one I just took!

259
00:15:59,040 --> 00:16:03,680
An attack with the intent to kill

260
00:16:03,680 --> 00:16:04,880
will come with a breath.

261
00:16:05,480 --> 00:16:06,560
The breath of life.

262
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:09,420
I refuse to get anywhere near you

263
00:16:09,420 --> 00:16:11,740
until you let one of my shimmers distract you

264
00:16:11,740 --> 00:16:13,180
and give me an opening.

265
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:15,740
The instant I see that opening,

266
00:16:16,200 --> 00:16:17,820
my blade will leap from the shadows

267
00:16:17,820 --> 00:16:19,060
and pierce your throat.

268
00:16:19,880 --> 00:16:21,040
But first...

269
00:16:21,040 --> 00:16:24,340
The breath of life!

270
00:16:24,960 --> 00:16:26,580
The eye caliber attack!

271
00:16:38,500 --> 00:16:39,940
What was that for?

272
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:41,000
Were you trying to kill me

273
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,340
just because you heard me breathing?

274
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:46,020
I'm a samurai knight.

275
00:16:46,440 --> 00:16:47,820
My blade knows its enemies.

276
00:16:51,040 --> 00:16:52,200
No.

277
00:16:52,800 --> 00:16:54,200
How did you...

278
00:16:54,200 --> 00:16:57,040
I heard his breath.

279
00:16:57,240 --> 00:16:58,620
While he thought I was distracted,

280
00:16:58,900 --> 00:17:00,600
he tried to sneak up and stab you.

281
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:03,140
That villain is a knave to his core.

282
00:17:04,040 --> 00:17:04,600
Can you stand?

283
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:07,640
Impressive work, Arthur.

284
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:11,900
Where'd the other one go?

285
00:17:12,420 --> 00:17:14,240
I think he ditched his pal and ran off.

286
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:17,020
What was up with that one's face?

287
00:17:17,620 --> 00:17:18,520
Think he's human?

288
00:17:18,520 --> 00:17:22,600
The man's face was somewhat mask-like.

289
00:17:22,820 --> 00:17:24,160
But what would he be if not a human?

290
00:17:25,940 --> 00:17:26,340
Hmm.

291
00:17:33,180 --> 00:17:34,760
We need to rejoin the others.

292
00:17:35,300 --> 00:17:36,400
Great. Lead the way.

293
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:41,780
So it goes.

294
00:17:41,780 --> 00:17:47,980
Looks like the tunnel forks off again.

295
00:17:48,500 --> 00:17:49,140
This sucks.

296
00:17:49,380 --> 00:17:51,460
Why is the nether confusing and scary?

297
00:17:52,080 --> 00:17:54,400
Have any ideas about which way we should try?

298
00:17:57,880 --> 00:17:59,340
Do you see what I see?

299
00:17:59,920 --> 00:18:02,000
There's something glowing on the left side.

300
00:18:05,240 --> 00:18:05,960
Two days!

301
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:07,440
And they're coming toward us!

302
00:18:07,780 --> 00:18:08,520
They're...

303
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:09,360
My eyes!

304
00:18:09,360 --> 00:18:16,480
Who are you calling an over-dice tunnel troll?

305
00:18:16,660 --> 00:18:18,360
We never said that, we swear!

306
00:18:19,680 --> 00:18:20,180
Oh, hey.

307
00:18:20,660 --> 00:18:21,680
It's you, Maki.

308
00:18:22,620 --> 00:18:24,360
So those demonic eyes were just...

309
00:18:25,220 --> 00:18:27,340
Sputter and flare.

310
00:18:28,660 --> 00:18:29,100
Maki!

311
00:18:29,740 --> 00:18:31,280
It's super scary down here!

312
00:18:31,280 --> 00:18:31,720
There, there.

313
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:32,760
You'll be safe with me.

314
00:18:32,760 --> 00:18:40,640
Two life signs just showed up out of nowhere.

315
00:18:41,300 --> 00:18:42,580
They're 15 meters away.

316
00:18:42,820 --> 00:18:44,000
We should be able to see them.

317
00:18:44,640 --> 00:18:45,620
Are they on our side?

318
00:18:46,180 --> 00:18:50,060
You will never see a person who is on your side again.

319
00:18:50,060 --> 00:18:58,320
Hey, Lisa.

320
00:18:58,320 --> 00:19:03,220
So you finally gave up and put on the uniform you despised.

321
00:19:03,860 --> 00:19:05,680
You look like a fool in it, Vulcan.

322
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:06,920
You know that, right?

323
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:11,820
And you look great in whatever you wear.

324
00:19:13,820 --> 00:19:16,240
You've always hated the Fire Force more than anything.

325
00:19:16,720 --> 00:19:18,480
So what would make you follow them underground?

326
00:19:18,900 --> 00:19:20,080
How is that a question?

327
00:19:20,380 --> 00:19:22,780
I obviously came down here to see you, Lisa.

328
00:19:22,780 --> 00:19:30,140
What's the matter, feeler?

329
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:34,760
Are you forgetting who it was that gave you a home?

330
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:38,700
Who accepted a filthy, ignorant cat like you?

331
00:19:38,980 --> 00:19:41,120
And taught you everything you know?

332
00:19:41,540 --> 00:19:43,960
Who showed you how to manipulate fire?

333
00:19:44,420 --> 00:19:46,080
How to manipulate men?

334
00:19:47,080 --> 00:19:50,900
You only gained Vulcan's affection by using the techniques I taught you.

335
00:19:50,900 --> 00:19:53,920
He only took you in because you followed my teachings.

336
00:19:54,640 --> 00:19:56,180
Without me, you are nothing.

337
00:19:56,760 --> 00:19:59,340
Nothing but a stupid, dirty cat.

338
00:20:00,600 --> 00:20:03,140
Understand, or do you need another lesson?

339
00:20:03,560 --> 00:20:05,120
Get the hell away from her!

340
00:20:17,380 --> 00:20:19,620
You should know my true name is Fila.

341
00:20:19,620 --> 00:20:22,760
And that I am a knight of the Ashen Flames.

342
00:20:26,860 --> 00:20:27,840
That's right.

343
00:20:28,260 --> 00:20:29,820
Protect me with your life.

344
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:30,500
Yes, sir.

345
00:20:30,780 --> 00:20:32,340
He's lying to you, damn it!

346
00:20:32,760 --> 00:20:33,460
Shut up!

347
00:20:35,240 --> 00:20:36,540
The Iron Matillo?

348
00:20:37,320 --> 00:20:41,020
Something tells me that your lessons did Lisa more harm than good.

349
00:20:41,020 --> 00:20:45,220
But regardless, teaching the youth is just what grown-ups do.

350
00:20:45,740 --> 00:20:48,260
So stop pretending she owes you, you geezer!

351
00:20:50,160 --> 00:20:52,580
Come to think of it, you're quite ignorant too.

352
00:20:53,160 --> 00:20:54,720
Feckless captain of the eighth.

353
00:20:55,300 --> 00:20:57,020
You can call me what you want.

354
00:20:57,260 --> 00:21:00,260
You don't even know what the flames of human combustion are.

355
00:21:00,260 --> 00:21:05,400
But our evangelist knows everything.

356
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:12,760
Why the spontaneous human combustion phenomenon is assaulting our world.

357
00:21:13,540 --> 00:21:17,800
The true nature of the bugs that have created artificial infernals.

358
00:21:17,800 --> 00:21:21,680
The secret behind Shinra Kusukabe's Adola Burst.

359
00:21:22,880 --> 00:21:26,820
Why his fire is known to us as the flame of perdition.

360
00:21:27,360 --> 00:21:29,480
What happened to this world in the past?

361
00:21:30,820 --> 00:21:33,640
And what is happening to it as we speak?

362
00:21:34,940 --> 00:21:38,140
The evangelist knows all this and more.

363
00:21:38,140 --> 00:21:41,740
But I will not share that knowledge.

364
00:21:44,420 --> 00:21:47,400
It sounds like you really are a lousy teacher.

365
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:52,020
You're an intriguing man.

366
00:22:08,140 --> 00:22:38,120
I will not share that knowledge.

367
